### DCC API — requests you can run from Visual Studio (or VS Code's REST Client).
### 1. Run "Sign in" with the admin's email and password (Server/.local/initial-admin.txt).
### 2. Copy "accessToken" from the answer into @token below.
### 3. On first sign-in, change the password first — everything else answers 403 until you do.

@api = http://localhost:5080
@token = paste-the-access-token-here

### Sign in
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@dcc.local", "password": "paste-the-password-here" }

### Change your password (required on first sign-in; at least 12 characters)
POST {{api}}/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currentPassword": "the-current-one", "newPassword": "a-new-long-password" }

### Who am I, and what may I do
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── users ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### All users
GET {{api}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a user with an initial password (they must change it on first sign-in)
POST {{api}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "dana@example.com", "displayName": "Dana", "kind": "person", "password": "initial-password-123" }

### Disable a user (their sessions end at once)
PATCH {{api}}/users/USER-ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "disabled": true }

### ── security roles and assignments ──────────────────────────────────

### The permission catalog
GET {{api}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Security roles (built-in and custom)
GET {{api}}/security-roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Give a user a security role on one client (scopeType: global | client | requirement)
POST {{api}}/role-assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "principalType": "user", "principalId": "USER-ID", "securityRoleId": "ROLE-ID", "scopeType": "client", "scopeId": "CLIENT-ID" }

### Who holds what
GET {{api}}/role-assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Take an assignment away (takes effect at once)
DELETE {{api}}/role-assignments/ASSIGNMENT-ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── teams ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Create a team
POST {{api}}/teams
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "QA", "description": "Testers" }

### Add a member
PUT {{api}}/teams/TEAM-ID/members/USER-ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── agents and API tokens ───────────────────────────────────────────

### Create a delegated AI agent (acts for you, never more than you may)
POST {{api}}/agents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "displayName": "Build bot" }

### Create an API token for the agent — the secret is shown only in this answer
POST {{api}}/tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "build bot on CI", "forAgentId": "AGENT-ID" }

### ── audit ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Every change to identity and permissions, newest first
GET {{api}}/identity-audit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── tasks ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Propose tasks on a requirement (the second waits for the first)
POST {{api}}/workitems/REQUIREMENT-ID/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tasks": [ { "intent": "Add the discount table", "appetite": "small" }, { "intent": "Apply the discount at checkout", "dependsOn": [0] } ] }

### The tree, its schedule and every card's status
GET {{api}}/workitems/REQUIREMENT-ID/task-flow
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Approve a task — its checklist with it; it goes to TFS at once when a connection exists
POST {{api}}/tasks/TASK-ID/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### What a run would send to Claude (never runs it)
GET {{api}}/tasks/TASK-ID/implement-preview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Develop the task with Claude, on DCC's own copy of the repository (commits locally, never pushes)
POST {{api}}/tasks/TASK-ID/implement
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The live transcript of its run
GET {{api}}/tasks/TASK-ID/flow-run
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The task's whole page: status, steps, development, checks, runs
GET {{api}}/tasks/TASK-ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
